          "text": "CHIANG Yüeh-kuang 姜曰廣 (T. 居之, H. 燕及), d. Mar. 1, 1649, Ming statesman, was a native of Hsin-chien, Kiangsi. A chin-shih of 1619, he was appointed to the Hanlin Academy and became a compiler.",
